@* Batch F2, 6-ARCH ("every passage entry is expandable IN PLACE to read the
   whole chapter -- REUSE Batch R's mini-reader... not a reimplementation"):
   the expand/collapse + lazy chapter-fetch + auto-scroll + place-mention
   blink MECHANISM Batch R's VerseTextSection.razor introduced, extracted
   here so every passage entry in the popover platform (cross-references,
   THE SCRIPTURES, place est/dest -- PassageList.razor) can open its OWN
   independent mini-reader, not just the verse-text section's single
   instance. VerseTextSection.razor itself now wraps THIS component (see
   its own comment) -- one mechanism, every caller.

   O2 (owner live-preview correction, 2026-08-23: "we have redundant
   buttons... Show the rest of this passage and Read the whole chapter...
   get rid of the read the whole chapter and replace with just a down/
   double down arrow that manages expansion/collapsing"): the expand
   trigger below used to be a single `popover-verse-expand` TEXT button
   (one element, three labels depending on state -- "Read the whole
   chapter"/"+N more -- read the chapter"/"Show just this verse"),
   toggling `_expanded` itself. That button, and PassageList.razor's own
   SEPARATE per-entry `popover-passage-clamp-expand/-collapse` toggle that
   used to sit alongside it on the SAME entry (the "redundant pair" the
   owner named), are BOTH retired -- replaced by ONE RevealControls
   instance below, the SAME shared reveal component U2/R-D3 already
   established for xrefs/catechism, reused here (not reimplemented) for a
   genuinely BINARY case: Default=0/Total=1/Step=1, so "Shown" is just
   `_expanded` as 0-or-1. This is the one place the underlying "how many
   verses of the passage's own CLAMPED text are showing" nuance
   PassageList's old per-entry clamp toggle offered is honestly lost --
   revealing ANY more now always means the full lazy-fetched chapter, never
   a partial reveal of just the clamped entry's own remaining verses -- a
   disclosed simplification in service of "ONE expansion idiom," not an
   oversight (PassageList.razor's own STATIC clamp -- how many verses show
   BEFORE either arrow is ever touched -- is unaffected; see that file's
   own comment). RevealNoun/MoreLabel/CollapseLabel below supply this
   binary case's own verbatim copy -- see RevealControls.razor's own O2
   paragraph for why the generic "{N} more {RevealNoun}" template doesn't
   fit a chapter. TestIdSuffix, PassageList.razor's own multi-instance
   discipline (see below), extends naturally to the new CollapseTestId too.

   TestIdSuffix lets multiple instances coexist in one popover without
   colliding testids: "" (VerseTextSection's own usage) reproduces the
   EXACT original bare testids (popover-verse-expand/-reader/-reader-verse-{n})
   byte for byte, so nothing that already asserts against those breaks;
   a non-empty suffix (PassageList.razor passes "-{entry.TestId}", that
   entry's own FULL already-prefixed testid, e.g. "-xref-item-GEN.1.1-3" --
   NOT a bare span; fix-round-1 correction, this comment previously said
   "each block's own span" -- see CONTRACT.md's own popover-verse-expand
   note) scopes a NEW instance's own controls uniquely, and carries that
   entry's own repeated-span disambiguation (--2/--3) along with it. *@
@using BibleAtlas.Client.Explore
@inject AtlasClient Atlas
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@inject ViewStateService ViewState

@if (!_expanded)
{
    @CompactContent
}
else
{
    <div class="popover-reader" data-testid="@($"popover-verse-reader{TestIdSuffix}")" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
        @if (_error is not null)
        {
            <p class="popover-meta">@_error</p>
        }
        else if (_chapter is null)
        {
            <p class="popover-meta">Loading&hellip;</p>
        }
        else
        {
            @foreach (var v in _chapter.Verses)
            {
                var isFocal = v.Verse >= FocalFromVerse && v.Verse <= FocalToVerse;
                <div class="popover-reader-verse" data-testid="@($"popover-reader-verse-{v.Verse}{TestIdSuffix}")" data-focal="@(isFocal ? "true" : "false")"
                     id="@(v.Verse == FocalFromVerse ? _focalDomId : null)">
                    <span class="popover-reader-verse-num">@v.Verse</span>
                    <span class="popover-reader-verse-text">
                        @foreach (var seg in PlaceMentions.Scan(v.Text, v.Places, v.Persons))
                        {
                            @if (seg.PlaceId is { } placeId)
                            {
                                <span class="popover-reader-mention" data-testid="@($"popover-reader-mention-{v.Verse}-{placeId}{TestIdSuffix}")"
                                      tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="@($"Explore {seg.PlaceName}")"
                                      @onpointerenter="() => Blink(placeId, true)" @onpointerleave="() => Blink(placeId, false)"
                                      @onfocus="() => Blink(placeId, true)" @onblur="() => Blink(placeId, false)"
                                      @onclick="() => OpenPlace(placeId, seg.PlaceName!)" @onclick:stopPropagation="true"
                                      @onkeydown="@(e => OnPlaceMentionKeyDown(e, placeId, seg.PlaceName!))" @onkeydown:stopPropagation="true">@seg.Text</span>
                            }
                            else if (seg.PersonId is { } personId)
                            {
                                <span class="popover-reader-mention popover-reader-mention-person" data-testid="@($"popover-reader-mention-person-{v.Verse}-{personId}{TestIdSuffix}")"
                                      tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="@($"Explore {seg.PersonName}")"
                                      @onclick="() => OpenPerson(personId, seg.PersonName!)" @onclick:stopPropagation="true"
                                      @onkeydown="@(e => OnPersonMentionKeyDown(e, personId, seg.PersonName!))" @onkeydown:stopPropagation="true">@seg.Text</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                @seg.Text
                            }
                        }
                    </span>
                </div>
            }
        }
    </div>
}

@* M-D3/U6, owner verbatim: "'read the whole chapter' affordance REMOVED
   when already reading that chapter" -- conditional presence, not a
   disabled stub: when the reader is ACTIVELY showing this exact
   Book/Chapter right now (ViewStateService.MountedReaderChapter's own doc
   comment has the full "why not the persistent ViewState.Reader" story),
   the whole control is absent, never merely inert -- reading the SAME
   content it would open is already on screen, so there is nothing left for
   it to honestly offer (the compact preview above still renders exactly as
   before; only this one affordance disappears). _expanded can never become
   true in this state, by construction -- this control is the only thing
   that ever sets it. *@
@if (!AlreadyInCurrentReaderChapter)
{
    <RevealControls Total="1" Default="0" Step="1" Shown="@(_expanded ? 1 : 0)" ShownChanged="OnShownChanged"
                     MoreTestId="@($"popover-verse-expand{TestIdSuffix}")" CollapseTestId="@($"popover-verse-collapse{TestIdSuffix}")"
                     RevealNoun="verses"
                     MoreLabel="@(TruncatedBy > 0 ? $"+{TruncatedBy} more — read the chapter" : "Read the whole chapter")"
                     CollapseLabel="Show just this verse" />
}

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Book { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public int Chapter { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public int FocalFromVerse { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public int FocalToVerse { get; set; }
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment CompactContent { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public string TestIdSuffix { get; set; } = "";

    // M-D3/U5 (in-text mentions-attested links): the SAME "a provider/caller
    // supplies ctx.PushAsync, this component only ever calls OnExplore"
    // contract PassageList.razor's own OnExplore already establishes --
    // required, not optional, matching that precedent (both of this
    // component's two real callers, PassageList.razor and
    // VerseTextSection.razor, always have a real ctx.PushAsync in hand to
    // supply). Threads a mention click (place OR person, see OpenPlace/
    // OpenPerson below) up to whichever popover this mini-reader instance
    // is currently rendering inside.
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback<IExplorable> OnExplore { get; set; }

    // M-D3/U6: read fresh at RENDER time (a computed property, not cached
    // state) -- ViewState.MountedReaderChapter can change out from under an
    // already-open popover (e.g. chapter navigation while a split-view
    // popover sits open on the atlas pane), and this must always reflect
    // the CURRENT truth, the same "read live context at render time, never
    // captured once" discipline CAP-RECONCILE-1's own OtherContextSectionCount/
    // XrefEntryPoint already establish elsewhere in this popover platform.
    private bool AlreadyInCurrentReaderChapter =>
        ViewState.MountedReaderChapter is { } cur && cur.Book == Book && cur.Chapter == Chapter;

    // Batch HOTFIX-4 requirement 7 (honest truncation signal, W2 review
    // Important-1: "VerseGroup.Count ships on the wire but the client
    // never reads it"): when >0, the COLLAPSED control's own MoreLabel
    // becomes "+{N} more — read the chapter" instead of the plain "Read
    // the whole chapter" -- SAME control, SAME testid, SAME click handler
    // (opens the identical full-chapter reader below; "wired to the
    // existing MiniReaderExpand," no parallel affordance). The
    // EXPANDED-state label ("Show just this verse") is unaffected -- once
    // the reader is open, the true content is already visible, nothing
    // left to signal.
    [Parameter] public int TruncatedBy { get; set; }

    private bool _expanded;
    private ChapterOut? _chapter;
    private string? _error;
    private bool _scrolledThisExpand;
    private IJSObjectReference? _readerJs;

    // A random, per-component-instance DOM id for the focal row -- see
    // VerseTextSection.razor's own original comment (preserved verbatim in
    // spirit): collision-safe by construction (a fresh GUID per instance),
    // never needs TestIdSuffix.
    private readonly string _focalDomId = $"popover-reader-focal-{Guid.NewGuid():N}";

    // "Fetch on expand, not before" -- the whole chapter is only ever
    // requested once the user actually asks to read it, via AtlasClient's
    // own Chapter LRU cache (so re-expanding after a collapse, or a later
    // expand of a DIFFERENT block in the same chapter, is free).
    //
    // O2: RevealControls' own ShownChanged always proposes a fully-
    // determined target (0 or 1 here, this component's own binary case --
    // see this file's own header comment), never a relative toggle, so this
    // is `shown == 1` directly rather than the old `!_expanded` inversion --
    // otherwise byte-for-byte the same fetch-on-expand body the retired
    // ToggleExpand() always had.
    private async Task OnShownChanged(int shown)
    {
        _expanded = shown == 1;
        if (_expanded && _chapter is null)
        {
            _error = null;
            try
            {
                _chapter = await Atlas.Chapter(Book, Chapter);
            }
            catch (Exception)
            {
                _error = "Couldn't load the chapter — check your connection and try again.";
            }
        }

        if (_expanded)
        {
            _scrolledThisExpand = false; // OnAfterRenderAsync below performs the actual scroll once the focal row exists in the DOM
        }
    }

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!_expanded || _scrolledThisExpand || _chapter is null || _error is not null)
        {
            return;
        }

        _scrolledThisExpand = true;
        try
        {
            _readerJs ??= await JS.InvokeAsync<IJSObjectReference>("import", "./js/reader.js");
            await _readerJs.InvokeVoidAsync("scrollFocalRowIntoView", _focalDomId);
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // The auto-scroll is a nicety, not load-bearing -- the mini-reader
            // still renders and is manually scrollable either way.
        }
    }

    // Toggles the SAME map.js blinkPlace every currently-live map instance
    // (full /world, or a split view's own embedded pane) responds to -- see
    // MapInterop.BlinkPlace's own doc comment for why this needs no
    // reference to any specific map/component at all.
    private Task Blink(string placeId, bool active) => MapInterop.BlinkPlace(JS, placeId, active);

    // M-D3/U5: a mention click pushes the SAME node kind its own popover
    // section would, onto the SAME popover stack (OnExplore, above) -- click
    // and hover-blink are independent, both always available on a place
    // mention (a click doesn't cancel/replace the blink the pointer/focus
    // handlers above already own). PlaceNode's own id stays bare (the
    // LEGACY AtlasData-backed convention every other PlaceNode construction
    // site in this app already uses -- World.razor's OpenPlaceFromCard,
    // PopoverSectionProviders' own place-row buttons).
    private Task OpenPlace(string placeId, string placeName) => OnExplore.InvokeAsync(new PlaceNode(placeId, placeName));

    // PersonRefDto.Id (VerseOut.Persons, the chapter-view's own attested-
    // mentions index) is the graph's RAW node id ("aaron_1") -- UNLIKE the
    // generic edges page's own NodeRefDto.Id, which already carries the
    // "Person:" wire prefix (see PersonCardAndMentionsSection's own persons-
    // list buttons, PopoverSectionProviders.cs). PersonNode always stores
    // (and later threads verbatim into ctx.Graph.Card/.Edges) the WIRE
    // form, so this is the one place that prefix gets added, matching
    // PersonNode's own doc comment example ("Person:aaron_1") exactly.
    private Task OpenPerson(string personId, string personName) => OnExplore.InvokeAsync(new PersonNode($"Person:{personId}", personName));

    // "Enter opens" -- the same scope, and the same bespoke-named-method-
    // per-target shape, every other explorable element in this app uses
    // (PassageList.razor's own OnKeyDown, Reader.razor's OnVerseLineKeyDown/
    // OnHeadingKeyDown, PlaceCard's OnVerseKeyDown/OnPassageKeyDown).
    private Task OnPlaceMentionKeyDown(KeyboardEventArgs e, string placeId, string placeName) => e.Key == "Enter" ? OpenPlace(placeId, placeName) : Task.CompletedTask;
    private Task OnPersonMentionKeyDown(KeyboardEventArgs e, string personId, string personName) => e.Key == "Enter" ? OpenPerson(personId, personName) : Task.CompletedTask;
}
